<%- include('partials/head', { title, description, extraHead: '<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/reentry.css">' }) %>
<body>
<%- include('partials/header', { activePage }) %>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="reentry-page">

        <!-- Hero Header -->
        <section class="page-header reentry-hero">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="hero-badge">
                    <i class="fas fa-door-open"></i> Re-Entry Services
                </div>
                <h1>Re-Entry Services</h1>
                <p>Bridging the gap from incarceration to independence — comprehensive, trauma-informed support for returning citizens every step of the way</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Mission Statement -->
        <section class="mission-banner">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="mission-content">
                    <i class="fas fa-quote-left mission-quote-icon"></i>
                    <p>"Every person deserves the opportunity to heal, grow, and contribute. At Alase Center for Enrichment, we believe transformation is possible — with the right support, accountability, and compassion."</p>
                    <span class="mission-attribution">— Alase Center for Enrichment</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Re-Entry Services Section -->
        <section class="service-section reentry-section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="service-section-header">
                    <div class="service-section-icon">
                        <i class="fas fa-door-open"></i>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h2>How We Help Returning Citizens</h2>
                        <p class="service-subtitle">A comprehensive continuum of support from release to stability</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="service-intro">
                    <p>Returning to the community after incarceration is one of life's most challenging transitions. The first days, weeks, and months after release are critical — and the barriers are significant: lack of housing, employment history gaps, limited transportation, strained family relationships, and unresolved mental health or substance use issues can quickly derail even the most motivated individual.</p>
                    <p>At <strong>Alase Center for Enrichment</strong>, we provide a comprehensive, trauma-informed continuum of re-entry services designed to address these barriers head-on. Our experienced team of peer support specialists — many of whom have lived experience with incarceration — walks alongside returning citizens every step of the way.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="services-grid-detailed">
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-home"></i></div>
                        <h3>Transitional Housing Support</h3>
                        <p>We connect individuals with safe, stable transitional housing options and provide advocacy to overcome the barriers many returning citizens face in securing housing. We work with landlords, housing programs, and government resources to find suitable placements.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-briefcase"></i></div>
                        <h3>Employment Readiness</h3>
                        <p>Our employment coaches help participants build job-ready skills — from resume writing and interview preparation to identifying "ban-the-box" friendly employers and navigating background check disclosures. We help individuals present their strengths confidently.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-id-card"></i></div>
                        <h3>Documentation Assistance</h3>
                        <p>We assist with obtaining critical identification documents — state ID, Social Security cards, birth certificates — that are essential for accessing housing, employment, benefits, and other services.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-brain"></i></div>
                        <h3>Mental Health &amp; Substance Use Support</h3>
                        <p>Returning citizens often carry unresolved trauma, mental health conditions, and substance use challenges. We connect individuals with licensed mental health professionals and peer recovery coaches who provide culturally competent, trauma-informed care.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i></div>
                        <h3>Education &amp; Skills Training</h3>
                        <p>We help individuals explore educational opportunities — GED completion, vocational training, community college enrollment — and connect them with scholarship resources available to those with criminal records.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-users"></i></div>
                        <h3>Family Reunification &amp; Support</h3>
                        <p>We provide counseling and mediation services to help rebuild healthy family relationships. Strong family connections are one of the most powerful protective factors against recidivism.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale"></i></div>
                        <h3>Legal Navigation Support</h3>
                        <p>We help individuals understand their legal obligations during supervision (parole/probation), navigate compliance requirements, and connect with legal aid organizations for expungements, restoration of rights, and other legal needs.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="service-detail-card">
                        <div class="sdc-icon"><i class="fas fa-heartbeat"></i></div>
                        <h3>Peer Mentoring</h3>
                        <p>Our certified peer support specialists — individuals who have themselves navigated the criminal justice system and successfully rebuilt their lives — provide authentic, empathetic mentoring that no textbook can replicate. They are proof that change is possible.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Stats Banner -->
        <section class="stats-banner">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="stats-grid">
                    <div class="stat-block">
                        <h3>68%</h3>
                        <p>of released prisoners are rearrested within 3 years without proper support</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="stat-block">
                        <h3>↓ 50%</h3>
                        <p>reduction in recidivism with comprehensive re-entry support programs</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="stat-block">
                        <h3>700K+</h3>
                        <p>individuals are released from prison in the United States annually</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="stat-block">
                        <h3>$35,000</h3>
                        <p>average cost per year to incarcerate — prevention and re-entry support is more effective</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Why Choose Alase -->
        <section class="why-alase-section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <h2>Why Choose Alase for Re-Entry?</h2>
                    <p>What sets our re-entry programs apart</p>
                </div>
                <div class="why-grid">
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-microscope"></i><h3>Evidence-Based</h3><p>Our programs follow the Sequential Intercept Model and other proven frameworks grounded in current research.</p></div>
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-handshake"></i><h3>Peer-Led Support</h3><p>We pair clinical services with certified peer mentors who have lived experience — a combination that accelerates real change.</p></div>
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-heart"></i><h3>Trauma-Informed</h3><p>Every interaction is grounded in empathy, safety, and respect for each individual's unique journey and background.</p></div>
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-map-marker-alt"></i><h3>Community Connected</h3><p>Deep roots in North Carolina with relationships across housing providers, employers, and government agencies statewide.</p></div>
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-award"></i><h3>Clinically Led</h3><p>Overseen by Dr. Anthony Smith, PhD, bringing academic excellence and compassionate leadership to every program.</p></div>
                    <div class="why-card"><i class="fas fa-redo"></i><h3>Focused on Success</h3><p>Our ultimate measure is community safety and individual flourishing — not just program completion.</p></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Get Started CTA -->
        <section class="cta-section reentry-cta">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="cta-content">
                    <h2>Ready to Take the Next Step?</h2>
                    <p>Whether you're seeking services for yourself, a family member, or are a referring agency — we're here to help. Contact us today to learn more or schedule an intake assessment.</p>
                    <div class="cta-buttons">
                        <a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Us Today</a>
                        <a href="/resources" class="btn btn-secondary btn-outline">View Community Resources</a>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cta-contact-info">
                        <span><i class="fas fa-phone"></i> (919) 957-7357</span>
                        <span><i class="fas fa-envelope"></i> info@alase.org</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
